ursement-project/september-reimbursements.csv\u001b\\september-reimbursements.csv\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;255m\u001b[48;5;234m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\ --json   # for import\u001b[39m                                                                \u001b[49m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mThe filename is always required (built-in default is \u001b[48;5;234mexpenses.csv\u001b[49m, which isn't here).\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;252mExcluded rows \u2014 none silently included.\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;252m Three rows have non-numeric amounts and are \u001b[3mnot\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252min any total: line 6 \u001b[48;5;234mNaN\u001b[49m (food), line 7 \u001b[48;5;234mInfinity\u001b[49m (travel), line 8 \u001b[48;5;234mtypo\u001b[49m (food). The tool\u001b[39m                                                  \u001b[38;5;252m\u276e\r\n\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;5;252mrejects them (no coercion), prints \u001b[48;5;234mseptember-reimbursements.csv:<line>: skipping invalid\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[48;5;234mamount '<value>'\u001b[49m to stderr, keeps the report on stdout clean, and exits \u001b[1m2\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;252m. So 160.00\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mcovers only the five valid rows. Someone must supply the real amounts for lines 6\u20138 or\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mconfirm they stay out \u2014 until then the total is provisional. Fix the CSV and re-run\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mrather than adjusting totals by hand.\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;252mVerified:\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;252m ran both the text and \u001b[48;5;234m--json\u001b[49m commands on the actual CSV (confirmed the three\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mskip warnings and exit 2, clean stdout), validated the JSON, and confirmed\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[4m\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/codeaf-sustained-1607/final/reimbursement-project/september-reimbursements.csv\u001b\\september-reimbursements.csv\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\ is unmodified.\u001b[39m\